-# iris-mlir
+# Iris compiler support and experimental simulator integration
 
-Merlin support for **Iris** (chipyard `iris-cy`, `IrisConfig`). This repository is a layer on top of
-[`rvv-mlir`](https://github.com/ucb-bar/rvv-mlir). It inherits all of RVV and adds Iris's configuration,
-its boards, and its **VME/Xsfmm matrix unit**.
+This package targets Chipyard `b4542facf6cc9457f6e358e8f80a8b3a0ff5df19`,
+Saturn `536774bd4c5e3bcd7813a4a0dc72fc87e5818532` and Rocket
+`fc745a8c377fdbf1d278eea81da9ac47b4b5fbc0`. Source hashes, local patches and
+elaboration evidence are retained in `source-identity.json`. Deployed bitstream
+association and RTL timing certification remain unverified.
 
-```
-rvv-mlir   (RVV contract, schedules)
- ├── kodiak-mlir   (+ BME OPU, + Kodiak boards)
- └── iris-mlir     (+ VME matrix unit, + Iris boards)    <- this repo
+The implementation baseline is Iris OOT
+`8447703ae5805271911e8ef232d8fd1aa7b6947d`, layered over RVV support
+`a80eea3eb749e5fd4cb822779a08d0d8ca09e5d5`. The companion Merlin baseline is
+`d56133b168bbee3d73cb8b4304d3622d4191fc6a`. The local integration requires its
+recorded patch; current upstream Merlin does not implement this OOT revision's
+originally advertised helper APIs.
+
+| Physical hart | Core | VLEN | DLEN | Operations |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---|
+| 0, 1 | Shuttle + Saturn | 256 | 128 | RVV integer, IEEE FP16/32/64, configured FP8/BF16 conversion/FMA subset, VME int8 and FP8 matrix |
+| 2 | Rocket + Saturn | 256 | 256 | RVV integer and IEEE FP16/32/64; no VME or MX FP8/BF16 arithmetic |
+
+The compiler kernel route implemented here is signed int8 to int32. Hardware FP8
+support does not imply a compiler FP8 lowering. The advertised scalar BF16 FCVT
+extension is absent from the actual scalar decoder; the model rejects those
+instructions. Consult the datatype audit for operation-specific format rules.
+
+## Source-derived kernel gate
+
+`source_facts.py` reads the enabled `opuInsns`, Saturn decode keys and whole
+Rocket matrix configuration BitPats. Every emitted instruction is independently
+cross-checked against the named declaration in the pinned `vme.h`. Receipt
+entries retain file SHA256 and source lines. Unread or unsupported syntax refuses
+emission. VLEN/DLEN are read from the OPU-enabled Shuttle configuration, and
+matrix types/kmax from their actual declarations. No instruction words are
+copied from the legacy simulator pin.
+
+`examples/iris/run.sh` is the concrete equivalent of the previously requested
+but absent Merlin `examples/iris/run.sh`. It builds the real OOT VME kernel and
+its scalar twin through Merlin's explicit caller-workspace pointer ABI. It
+compares every int32 accumulator and every W8A8 result with independent host
+semantics, and audits actual executable instructions. The fixture shapes are
+explicit: GEMM M=64,N=64,K=64; convolution NHWC[1,10,10,8] with HWIO[3,3,8,64],
+valid stride 1, yielding M=64,N=64,K=72. Guest im2col is included in convolution
+regions. GEMM `--shape M,N,K` permits independent edge/tail cases within the
+full-value output budget. These are newly declared source fixtures: no missing
+historical example's dimensions are silently assumed.
+
