-## The VME route
+The simulator is the verified Iris overlay on upstream Spike
+`72958551566a30f19444bd7e354552824e4d0a98`. The provider checks the actual
+binary, source overlay, selftests and evidence closure through iris-model's
+real provider. `configure_model.py` also runs a fresh 12-region three-hart smoke
+through the physical boot path. Any changed model input invalidates the selected
+manifest: regenerate it after a new verified model package. Legacy
+`MERLIN_SPIKE_ZVT` / `f90d5af...` never overrides this identity.
 
-int8 contractions `A(M,K)·B(K,N)` with a zero-initialised int32 accumulator, at least one tile in M and N,
-are rewritten by Merlin into calls to `merlin_vme_gemm_i8_<n>`. This package supplies what those resolve to:
+Execution is an explicit experimental functional opt-in. `MERLIN_IRIS_TIMING=on`
+is refused because no calibrated Iris timing model is available. Guest counters
+in these runs measure Spike instruction progress, not Iris cycle predictions.
+A successful gate establishes these concrete numerical kernel executions only.
 
