-Facts derived from the pinned sources (Merlin's `merlin/contract/hardware_pins.yaml`: `chipyard_iris`,
-`saturn_vme`, `rocket_chip_iris`, `spike_zvt`): TE = 32, operand alignment 16 B, matrix configurations
-(e8, w4) and (e32, w1), `kmax(8, 4) = 4`.
+A VME thread must first have a nonempty affinity wholly within harts 0/1 and
+call `iris_vme_enable()` once from thread context. That call explicitly zeros all
+four tiles and clobbers vector configuration. Registered tasks preserve FP/RVV,
+matrix configuration and all 16 KiB tile state across scheduling and 0/1
