+`compile_model.py` consumes ordinary linalg-on-tensors MLIR, invokes Merlin's
+actual contraction rewrite through this OOT, lowers through the LLVM23 Python
+runner, and compiles real RV64 objects. The generic descriptor bridge is emitted
+in LLVM IR, so its flattened memref arguments and aggregate return exactly match
+the upstream external function type instead of assuming a C struct/sret ABI.
+Rank2 and rank3 upstream/native ABI tests pass. Each call allocates/frees its own
+packing workspace. `_mlir_ciface_forward` fills the caller's output buffer and
+keeps intermediate allocation ownership inside the lowered program.
 
