+Use `op conv2d` and `--harts 1` for the other gates. The compiler input for
+convolution is explicitly its im2col contraction endpoint; the target-owned
+Zephyr producer compiles and executes the convolution indexing/packing. The
+whole convolution pipeline is checked against a direct independent convolution
+golden. No claim is made that the compiler captured a full framework convolution
+or an entire language model.
+
+All four GEMM/conv2d by one/two worker gates passed with three physical harts,
+three changing-input jobs, the real shipped VME kernel and scalar twin. Each
+image matched all 12,288 int32 values and 12,288 W8A8 values. The hart2 producer
+also passed its independent RVV checksum and overlapped computation. Final
+receipts are under `build/zephyr-mlir-final/` and bind the retained simulator
+`0c0fd7785d3e7ba2785e2e9eabc0d0af719037ab2fa761b71bab33fe24a5f257`.
+The end-to-end entrypoint is demonstrated separately by
+`build/merlin-workflow/gemm-h2/results.json`.
+
+The supported multicore compiler path is this explicit registered-task pipeline.
+Merlin's general OpenMP worker pool does not invoke the target ownership API;
+`parallel_tiles=True` therefore fails early. Ordinary whole-model generation,
+model-wide numerical qualification, calibrated timing, +/-2% held-out accuracy,
+RTL/FPGA equivalence and full model residency remain separate unmet gates.
+
+The current verified experimental-functional memory package was also tested through the full front door: binary `db964603d91ffb19f7e63dde0e14397635b879559011f1da8acaf5ecd06319a8`, manifest `build/merlin-simulator-current-memory/manifest.json`, workflow receipt `build/merlin-workflow/current-memory-gemm-h2/results.json`. Historical0c0 compiler evidence and its58-object input closure remain retained. The quantized output rule is the public Merlin integer epilogue `Tensor.requant(10).to_i8()` (half-up arithmetic shift then signed8 saturation), independently cross-checked in `build/merlin-epilogue-crosscheck.json`; it is distinct from float-scale/RNE and model-quality validation.
